     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, which is about double the maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin (2,550 mg/day). Entering it could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nThe order may have been meant differently. For example, 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) is the top of the immediate-release range, and 1700 mg could have been a total daily dose split into two doses. Please check the intended dose with the prescribing physician or pharmacist.\n\nBecause this is a medication order, it needs to come from a licensed prescriber who has reviewed the patient's chart. If you send me the corrected dose, route, and frequency from that prescriber, I can enter it."
      }
